--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Netlib LP test problems
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Files:
  crates/sundial-mps/tests/fixtures/{afiro,adlittle,sc50a,sc50b,share2b}.mps
  web/public/instances/{afiro,adlittle,sc50a,sc50b,share2b}.mps
  (also every instance fetched into the gitignored bench/ directory by
   scripts/fetch_netlib.sh)

Source: the Netlib linear-programming test set, http://www.netlib.org/lp/
Retrieved in the compressed MPS ("emps") format and expanded with emps.c from
http://www.netlib.org/lp/data/emps.c — see scripts/fetch_netlib.sh.

The Netlib LP set is a long-standing public collection of LP benchmark problems,
assembled by David Gay and distributed by Netlib for use in optimization
research. Netlib does not attach an explicit license to these files; they have
been freely redistributed in solver test suites for decades by convention. They
are included here unmodified apart from emps decompression.

Note: crates/sundial-mps/tests/fixtures/corner_bounds.mps and corner_ranges.mps
are NOT from Netlib — they are original hand-written parser fixtures and are
covered by this project's own license.

