2. NYC TLC yellow-cab trip records
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

File: web/public/taxi/points.json (a derived extract, not the raw records)

Source: New York City Taxi & Limousine Commission (TLC) trip record data for
June 2015, published by the TLC as public data:
https://www.nyc.gov/site/tlc/about/tlc-trip-record-data.page

points.json contains only a derived, projected extract — 1,024 pickup points,
1,152 drop-off points, and 20,000 basemap points, reduced to normalized 2-D
coordinates. No trip, fare, medallion, or license identifiers are retained.

Reproducibility caveat: the TLC's 2022 Parquet migration re-encoded the entire
historical archive, including 2015, to zone IDs only, so the official host no
longer serves the exact GPS coordinates this extract was built from.
scripts/fetch_taxi.py therefore fetches a community-preserved mirror of the
pre-migration file from a third-party S3 bucket
(nyc-tlc-trip-records-pds.s3.amazonaws.com). That mirror is not operated by the
TLC and states no redistribution terms of its own; it is used on a best-effort
basis for reproducibility. The committed points.json is the canonical artifact.
